  '<p class="gd-p">Your booking is confirmed. A few things are left: your licence photos, a selfie and proof of coverage, a signature from each additional driver, and the deposit.</p><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-we-still-need-from-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What we still need from you</h2><p class="gd-p">While a request or booking is not complete, everything it still needs is in one list, <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, under the steps on <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b> and on the booking: one line for each thing, with its state and a small button. The red button of <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> is always the first thing to do.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Needed</td><td>Send it: press the button on the line</td></tr><tr><td>Not accepted</td><td>We could not accept what you sent: the reason is on the line, send it again</td></tr><tr><td>Under review</td><td>We have it and a person on our team is checking it</td></tr><tr><td>Done</td><td>Nothing more to do</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">The lines are what this booking needs: your licence (front and back) and a selfie for each driver, proof of coverage (not with the Protection Plan), signing and paying, the deposit, each additional driver accepting the terms, your date of birth and your home address. On the booking, the details the agreement needs are filled in right there, under <b class="gd-ui">Your details for the agreement</b>. Our reminders name the same things.</p><p class="gd-p">Each line says exactly what is missing. With your own insurance (OPCF 27) you send two pages: the <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> (the insurance card for your own car) and the <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b> of your policy. If one is missing, the line says which one (&quot;We have your OPCF 27 endorsement page. Still needed: your pink slip&quot;), and its button opens that upload with the page chosen. Next to each upload is an example picture of the page with the parts that must show circled: your name, the policy number, the dates, the insurer and, on the endorsement page, the OPCF 27 line. Find it in your insurer&#39;s app or website, in your email, or in your car&#39;s glovebox. Put it flat, get all four corners in the photo, and avoid glare.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-booking-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your booking page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking opens with a large photo of your car, its name, the status and a clock: &quot;Pickup in 2 days 4 h&quot;, or &quot;Return by Sun 7 PM&quot; while you have the car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b>, then your booking. The status is on the photo, for example Confirmed, with your booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under the photo: when and where you pick up and return the car (tap a place to open it in Maps), the kilometres included, the fuel rule and the deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b>, at the top, tells you the one thing still needed, with its red button, for example <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b>, and the time left before pickup. Under it, your steps: done, now (<b class="gd-ui">Your turn</b>) and later. When nothing is needed it says when and where to pick up the car, with <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Manage your trip holds <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Ask to change dates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Message us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a driver</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/972"><img src="/guides/img/renter-08-booking-confirmed-desktop-b5603da5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="972"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.4%;top:54.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.4%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.4%;top:76.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Money, on the right (below on a phone), shows what you paid and what is owing, part by part, with a <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> button when something is open and your receipts. <b class="gd-ui">Price details</b> opens every line of the price. The steps under <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> show how far along you are: approve the offer, sign and pay, licence and insurance, pick up, return, final statement. A step finished since your last visit ticks over as the bar moves.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-rental-step-by-step" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your rental, step by step</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Your rental, step by step</b> on your booking opens the walkthrough: the whole rental in four stages, Before pickup, At pickup, On the road and The return.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start the walkthrough</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Continue</b> once you have begun). The top shows how many steps are done and which stage you are at.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The step to do now is in black at the top. A task opens its page, for example <b class="gd-ui">Add your licence</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Sign the agreement</b>, and is ticked once it is done. A step to read (what to bring, where we meet, your own photos, the road rules, what to do if something goes wrong, how to bring the car back) has <b class="gd-ui">Got it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At pickup, the walk-around: we photograph the car with you and you sign the condition report on your phone. Once done, <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b> opens every photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every stage is listed below with its steps, so you can read ahead.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-upload-your-licence-selfie-and-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Upload your licence, selfie and coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">Do this at least 24 hours before pickup. It takes a few minutes with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, front: lay the licence on a dark surface with all four corners visible. Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> for a photo already on your phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, back: do the same for the back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Selfie with your licence: hold the licence beside your face, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take selfie</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Coverage for damage to the car: add what your option asks for, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> (a PDF works too). Not sure your credit card covers rentals? Use the card coverage checker first.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">While your booking still needs them, <b class="gd-ui">Your trips</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Upload your licence</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Upload proof of insurance</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Check if your credit card covers rentals</b>, and our request and offer emails link straight to the licence upload.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/verify</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1232"><img src="/guides/img/renter-09-verify-desktop-d20f668d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1232"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.5%;top:65.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:95.3%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Your option</th><th scope="col">What we need</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Option 1, OPCF 27 on your own policy</td><td>Your insurer, the policy number and its expiry (after your return date), then two pages: your <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> (the liability insurance card) and the <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b>, each a PDF or a photo. Send both before you pay: the payment opens once they are in.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 2, your credit card&#39;s rental coverage</td><td>Pay with that card: it must be a credit card (debit and prepaid cards are refused) in your name. Search for your card (the bank and the card&#39;s name) and pick it: the page tells you at once whether it covers this car (the card&#39;s value limit, the kinds of car it leaves out, the most days). Then tick and confirm. Not on the list? Tick <b class="gd-ui">My card is not on the list</b> and type its name: our team checks it. The card&#39;s benefits document is optional.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 3, the CarmaCars Protection Plan</td><td>Ask for it on your booking; we confirm it once it is active.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Which cards include rental car coverage? <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> lists them, with each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), its longest rental and a link to its guide. Most cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and some of our cars are priced higher. Only your card&#39;s issuer decides a claim: call the number on the back of your card before you rent.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A person checks your proof and approves it, or tells you what to fix. The car is handed over only once it is approved. Changing your option replaces the earlier proof. We remind you 48 and 24 hours before pickup while it is missing. We delete licence and face photos 90 days after your rental ends.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-additional-drivers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Additional drivers</h2><p class="gd-p">Each additional driver signs the agreement with their own link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When the agreement is ready, each driver with an email gets their own signing link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Copy their signing link</b> to send it yourself, or <b class="gd-ui">Send a new link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each driver adds their own licence photos and selfie, like you did.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Signing links expire after 72 hours. A new link ends the older one, so always send the newest.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-add-something-to-your-trip" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add something to your trip</h2><p class="gd-p">Until 24 hours before pickup (or the notice an add-on needs), add add-ons from your booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, under Add-ons, press <b class="gd-ui">Add something to your trip</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick the add-on you want. Its price shows below.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add and pay</b>. It is charged at once on the card you paid with, and shows on your booking and receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A chauffeur needs our confirmation: press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for it</b>. We confirm it and charge your card then.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No card on file for this booking? The add-on is added and waits for payment: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay for your add-ons</b> under Add-ons, enter a card and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>. It is charged at once; that card is not kept.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If you cancel, add-ons are refunded like the rest of your booking. Flowers and a chauffeur are not refunded once their notice before pickup has started.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-to-bring-to-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What to bring to pickup</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your original licence. A photo is not enough.</li><li>The card you paid with. The deposit is taken on it about an hour before pickup.</li><li>A few minutes to walk around the car with us. We photograph it together.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-check-in-yourself-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check in yourself (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">From 24 hours before pickup, <b class="gd-ui">Check in yourself</b> on your booking: take the photos of the car as you get it (pick them all at once from your camera roll: all sides, odometer, fuel gauge, inside, any damage), the odometer and the fuel. If your booking is ready, you are checked in at once; otherwise a team member confirms it. If you do not take the photos, we take them.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Confirm it is you</b> is an optional step on the same page: take a photo of your licence and a selfie at that moment. We compare them with the ones on your booking, so the car goes to you and nobody else. You can skip it, and it never holds up your check-in. The photos are deleted with your other licence and face photos, 90 days after your rental ends.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-we-change-your-coverage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If we change your coverage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">If your card does not cover the car, or you ask for the CarmaCars Protection Plan, our team can switch your booking for you. You get an email with what changed and the new total. On an offer you approve the new price. On a booking you have paid, any extra is sent to you as a secure payment link, or you pay it from your booking page. You then do not need to send a card coverage document. If you go back to your card, the booking page asks you to confirm it again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-accident-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your accident card</h2><p class="gd-p">Your booking shows your <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b>: what to do after an accident, and the coverage of this booking.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>With your own auto policy (OPCF 27): your insurer and policy number, as on the proof you uploaded.</li><li>With your credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider.</li><li>With the Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number, the claims phone and your plan reference.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Print it</b> to print the card at its size for the glovebox, or keep the page on your phone.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Your name and date of birth</h3><p class="gd-p">Set them in your profile. Once your licence is verified they must match it: a change is sent as a correction request, shown as waiting until our team checks it against your licence.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-your-card-does-not-cover-the-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If your card does not cover the car</h2><p class="gd-p">The page says why: the card has no rental car damage coverage, the car is worth more than the card&#39;s limit, the card leaves out this kind of car, or the rental is longer than the card allows. Pick another card from the list, or under &quot;How will the car be covered?&quot; choose <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 on my own auto policy</b> or the Protection Plan.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-change-my-protection" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change my protection</h2><p class="gd-p">How damage to the car is covered can be changed on your booking page, under <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b>, once you approve the offer and until you return the car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change my protection</b>. You see the three options with their prices: your own insurance (OPCF 27), your credit card&#39;s coverage, or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Credit card coverage: choose your card from our list. It counts only if that card covers this car, and you tick that you will pay with it. Otherwise, OPCF 27: tick that you will upload your policy (the pink slip and the endorsement page). Otherwise, the Protection Plan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The Protection Plan applies at once: pay the difference with <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on your booking. Moving off the Protection Plan needs your proof (a photo or PDF); our team checks it and the change applies once approved. You can withdraw the request while it waits.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">During your trip you can add the Protection Plan; your own insurance or card coverage is set before pickup. After damage is reported, the protection stays as it was.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-sharing-your-location-at-pickup-and-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sharing your location at pickup and return</h2><p class="gd-p">With your permission, the CarmaCars app or the website shares where you are with our team only two hours either side of your pickup and your return, so we can meet you. At any other time nothing is taken. Turn it off any time in <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Location on the live map</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-countdown-calendar-and-your-steps" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Countdown, calendar and your steps</h2><p class="gd-p">From your offer until the pickup, your booking page counts down to the pickup: days, hours, minutes and seconds. <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b> puts your pickup and return in Apple Calendar, Google Calendar, Outlook or any other calendar app. Under it, your steps from the request to the final statement: each one ticks when it is done (the line moves on to the next), and a tap on a step says what it means and where to do it.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('renter', 'rewards', 'chapter', 'after-your-trip', 'CarmaCars Rewards gives you points on every rental. Points come off the rental charge of a later booking, and more points bring a higher tier with perks. Open **Rewards** in the menu.

## What we send you

We email you, and the same message shows under **Account** > **Notifications**:

1. Welcome to CarmaCars Rewards: when your account is made or your first booking is confirmed. How it works, your points and the ways to earn.
2. Points earned: after a rental closes, a review, a referral or your birthday. What earned them, your balance and how far you are from the next tier.
3. A new tier: when you reach Gold, Platinum or Black, with what it gives you.
4. Your free rental day: at Black, with a button that opens a booking with the code already in the promo code box.
5. Before points end: 30 days and 7 days before, and before a free day code ends.
6. Offers you can stop at any time with the unsubscribe link: close to the next tier, points waiting a month after your last rental, the monthly statement on the 1st, and your birthday and holiday rewards.

## Birthday and holiday rewards

From Platinum up, a rental that starts near your birthday or on a holiday weekend costs less: Platinum 10%, Black 20% off the rental charge. The bigger one applies, never both. Sign in before you book and the price shows the line **Birthday reward** or **Holiday reward**.

1. Your birthday comes from your driver''s licence when we have it.
2. Otherwise, on **Rewards** or **Account** > **Profile**, choose the month and type the day (the year is optional), then press **Save my birthday**.
3. The holidays are the Ontario ones: New Year''s Day, Family Day, Good Friday, Victoria Day, Canada Day, Civic Holiday, Labour Day, Thanksgiving, Christmas Day and Boxing Day. The Rewards page lists the next ones with their pickup days.

> Tip: The reward is off the rental charge only, never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit, and not on bookings paid by an insurer.', 'Rewards', 'Points, tiers, the emails we send and the birthday and holiday rewards.',
  'CarmaCars Rewards gives you points on every rental. Points come off the rental charge of a later booking, and more points bring a higher tier with perks. Open **Rewards** in the menu.

## What we send you

We email you, and the same message shows under **Account** > **Notifications**:

1. Welcome to CarmaCars Rewards: when your account is made or your first booking is confirmed. How it works, your points and the ways to earn.
2. Points earned: after a rental closes, a review, a referral or your birthday. What earned them, your balance and how far you are from the next tier.
3. A new tier: when you reach Gold, Platinum or Black, with what it gives you.
4. Your free rental day: at Black, with a button that opens a booking with the code already in the promo code box.
5. Before points end: 30 days and 7 days before, and before a free day code ends.
6. Offers you can stop at any time with the unsubscribe link: close to the next tier, points waiting a month after your last rental, the monthly statement on the 1st, and your birthday and holiday rewards.

## Birthday and holiday rewards

From Platinum up, a rental that starts near your birthday or on a holiday weekend costs less: Platinum 10%, Black 20% off the rental charge. The bigger one applies, never both. Sign in before you book and the price shows the line **Birthday reward** or **Holiday reward**.

1. Your birthday comes from your driver''s licence when we have it.
2. Otherwise, on **Rewards** or **Account** > **Profile**, choose the month and type the day (the year is optional), then press **Save my birthday**.
3. The holidays are the Ontario ones: New Year''s Day, Family Day, Good Friday, Victoria Day, Canada Day, Civic Holiday, Labour Day, Thanksgiving, Christmas Day and Boxing Day. The Rewards page lists the next ones with their pickup days.

> Tip: The reward is off the rental charge only, never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit, and not on bookings paid by an insurer.

## The game in Rewards

Rewards has **Today''s game**: press **Play now** and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). Your points go straight to your Rewards balance. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.',
  '<p class="gd-p">CarmaCars Rewards gives you points on every rental. Points come off the rental charge of a later booking, and more points bring a higher tier with perks. Open <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b> in the menu.</p><section class="gd-task" id="rewards-what-we-send-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What we send you</h2><p class="gd-p">We email you, and the same message shows under <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome to CarmaCars Rewards: when your account is made or your first booking is confirmed. How it works, your points and the ways to earn.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Points earned: after a rental closes, a review, a referral or your birthday. What earned them, your balance and how far you are from the next tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A new tier: when you reach Gold, Platinum or Black, with what it gives you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your free rental day: at Black, with a button that opens a booking with the code already in the promo code box.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Before points end: 30 days and 7 days before, and before a free day code ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Offers you can stop at any time with the unsubscribe link: close to the next tier, points waiting a month after your last rental, the monthly statement on the 1st, and your birthday and holiday rewards.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="rewards-birthday-and-holiday-rewards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Birthday and holiday rewards</h2><p class="gd-p">From Platinum up, a rental that starts near your birthday or on a holiday weekend costs less: Platinum 10%, Black 20% off the rental charge. The bigger one applies, never both. Sign in before you book and the price shows the line <b class="gd-ui">Birthday reward</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Holiday reward</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Your birthday comes from your driver&#39;s licence when we have it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise, on <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, choose the month and type the day (the year is optional), then press <b class="gd-ui">Save my birthday</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The holidays are the Ontario ones: New Year&#39;s Day, Family Day, Good Friday, Victoria Day, Canada Day, Civic Holiday, Labour Day, Thanksgiving, Christmas Day and Boxing Day. The Rewards page lists the next ones with their pickup days.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The reward is off the rental charge only, never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit, and not on bookings paid by an insurer.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="rewards-the-game-in-rewards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The game in Rewards</h2><p class="gd-p">Rewards has <b class="gd-ui">Today&#39;s game</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Play now</b> and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). Your points go straight to your Rewards balance. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'apply-and-get-your-car-listed', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'You apply online in about ten minutes. We reply within one business day, set your terms, and walk you through the rest.

## Apply to list your car

1. Go to `carmacars.ca/list-your-car` and press **Apply to list your car**.
2. Start with your name, mobile and email, and your car: its VIN, or its year, make and model. Press **Continue**. From here every answer is saved as you type.
3. About you: individual or corporation, your address, licence and date of birth. Press **Continue to vehicles**.
4. For each car, type the VIN: your car is found as you type the last character (Edit if anything is wrong), then tap its colour and answer the rest. Signed in? Press **Take a photo** under Fill this from the ownership permit: the VIN, plate and colour fill in from a photo of your Ontario permit, for you to check. Use **Add another vehicle** for more cars.
5. Read how it will work, press **Continue**, then **Review**.
6. Press **Submit application**, then **Go to your owner portal**.

![](/guides/img/public-13-list-your-car-desktop-48bf4cb0.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 800; address: carmacars.ca/list-your-car; pins: 1 20.1 74.9")

> Tip: Need a break? Your answers are already saved. **Email me a link** sends you a link to finish later, on any device. If you stop part way, we may email you a link to finish too.

> Good to know: No car to add yet? On the vehicle step press **I''ll add my car later**, choose your password and press **Open my owner account**. Your owner portal opens with **Add your first car**: press it when you are ready, starting with the VIN.

## What happens next

Five steps take your car from your driveway to its first rental.

:::flow
Tell us about the car | We confirm fees and set your terms
Sign the agreements | Online, one for all your cars
One registry visit | We fill in the forms and come with you
Tracker and insurance | We install it and add the car
Photos and listing | Live within 1 business day
:::

1. Right after you apply, Home shows **Read your agreements**: both agreements, filled in from your application, marked "Terms pending approval". The fees and the Revenue Share read Pending approval until we set them, and the Sign button stays off.
2. When your terms are ready, Home shows **Check and sign**. Everything is filled in from your application: check the short list of key values (each has a **Fix** link) and open any document to read it in full.
3. Sign in a few steps: say you read the documents, initial the three confirmations, tick the two consents and draw your signature. Then press **Sign all**. A code to your phone or email is optional (**Verify by code**); it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on. One signature covers every document, in about two minutes.
4. Pay the upfront invoice: the first and last month''s insurance fee for each car (see chapter 4).
5. Upload what each car''s checklist asks for: the ownership permit, the lender''s permission if it is financed or leased, and insurance.
6. Sign Forms C and D (filled in for you) on screen, with your witnesses beside you on the same device: Form C with one witness, Form D with two (see chapter 5).

## If we need a little more

Sometimes we need one more document before we can approve your application, for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip.

1. You get an email, and Home shows "We need a little more" with the list and any note from our team.
2. Upload what is asked, or write Your answer, and press **Send my answer**.
3. We review it within 1 business day. Once we approve your application, you get an email and Home shows Check and sign.

No typing the VIN: press **Scan the barcode** and point your phone at the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN** and take a photo of it. Check the VIN shown before you continue.

**Photos:** on your car''s page, **Add photos** takes any number at once, in any order. We sort them, put the outside photos on our studio background and touch up the inside ones. Photos that fit no shot go in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**. At least 10 are needed.

## A fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars

For a corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars for a fixed amount a month. You pay CarmaCars no fees: no invoices, no debits.

1. Go to `carmacars.ca/list-your-car` and press **A corporation with a fleet? Lease your cars to us as a fleet supplier** (or choose **A corporation** in the application, then **Fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars**).
2. About you: the corporation''s legal name and number, its registered address, and the signing officer''s name and title.
3. For each car: type the VIN (the year, make and model fill in), then the plate, and mark the car **Regular** or **Troubled** (it needs work). Each tier shows its lease a month. The tier is set when you add the car and does not change.
4. Say who the car is registered to now: **My corporation**, **Me or another officer, personally** (it moves into your corporation), or **A seller: the corporation is buying it**. For the last two, enter the name and address on the ownership and the transfer or sale date.
5. Press **Continue**, check the review and press **Submit application**. The ServiceOntario forms each car needs are filled in for you at once, under **Documents**: the lease to CarmaCars (CarmaCars holds the plates while it leases the car) and, for a car not yet registered to your corporation, the transfer into it. A seller signs the transfer on the back of the ownership. Only the empty boxes are filled. Sign each one on screen under **Documents**, then print it and sign it in ink at ServiceOntario.
6. In your owner portal, open **Cars**, then each car, and upload its ownership (registration) copy.
7. We check each car. Once we approve it, it is on the lease at its tier and Home shows **Check and sign**: you sign the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Form B (the lease summary) in the owner portal, on screen (there is no paper option). Form D (the limited power of attorney) is in your Documents too: you sign it on screen with two witnesses beside you, and CarmaCars signs its Part 2 at the same moment.

> Good to know: Home and **Money** show **Your fleet lease**: each car, its tier, its lease a month and the next payment date. The lease is paid on the 10th for the month before, with your statement; the first payment comes at least one full month after the car goes on the lease, and part months are paid by the day. Add more cars from your owner portal the same way.

## Sign first, then cars

You sign your agreement before any car comes over. As soon as your profile has your legal or corporation name, your address and, for a corporation, the signing officer and title, your agreement is made from it: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement (with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement it relies on) if you lease cars to CarmaCars, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. No car is needed.

Your owner portal home shows six steps: Your profile, Sign the agreement, Add your cars, Photos and inspection, Approved, Delivered. The current step has one button; press it.

- **Sign the agreement.** Read and sign opens it, filled in from your profile. You sign once on screen; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment.
- **Add your cars.** One at a time, or as a list of VINs from Cars > Add cars from a VIN list (a fleet supplier gives each car its tier and plate there). Each car goes on Schedule A of your agreement as a numbered entry, and you confirm each batch with one signature (Confirm my cars). Its government forms are made at the same moment.
- A car is approved, delivered or rented only once your agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. If CarmaCars approved it before you signed, it goes through by itself the moment you sign.

### Your car''s steps, one at a time

Once a car is on its way, Home shows **Your next step** and each car''s page shows **Your car''s steps**: every step of its onboarding, the one thing to do now with its button, what to bring, where to go and how long it takes. You are emailed and texted when a step is yours.

- **The route.** *Transfer*: the car''s registration moves into CarmaCars'' name. *Co-Registrant*: CarmaCars is added beside you. *Lease*: your corporation keeps the car and leases it to CarmaCars (no title transfer). An individual who leases through a new Owner Corporation first sets it up: Incorporate now opens our online incorporation partner (about 20 minutes), then upload the certificate.
- **The steps.** Application, Terms approved, Agreements signed, Documents uploaded (your driver''s licence, both sides of the ownership permit, your insurance slip and, if the car is financed, the lender''s payout letter; a corporation gives its corporate documents), Ownership transfer, New registration uploaded, Plate and insurance on the fleet policy, Inspected and photographed, Listed.
- Ownership transfer. Press **Find a ServiceOntario centre**, book a time, then **I booked it** with the time and the centre. Bring your licence, the original ownership permit, proof of insurance, the filled Form A and transfer documents (Documents > Government forms), the Used Vehicle Information Package and the Safety Standards Certificate when the step lists them. You pay the registry''s charges at the counter unless your Vehicle Schedule says CarmaCars pays them. After the counter, tick that the fees are paid and press **Transfer done**, then upload the new ownership permit on the car''s page.
- A step that waits on CarmaCars says **With CarmaCars**: nothing to do on your side.
