s.ca/list-your-car</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/800"><img src="/guides/img/public-13-list-your-car-desktop-48bf4cb0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="800"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.1%;top:74.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Need a break? Your answers are already saved. <b class="gd-ui">Email me a link</b> sends you a link to finish later, on any device. If you stop part way, we may email you a link to finish too.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>No car to add yet? On the vehicle step press <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ll add my car later</b>, choose your password and press <b class="gd-ui">Open my owner account</b>. Your owner portal opens with <b class="gd-ui">Add your first car</b>: press it when you are ready, starting with the VIN.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-what-happens-next" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What happens next</h2><p class="gd-p">Five steps take your car from your driveway to its first rental.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Tell us about the car</span><em>We confirm fees and set your terms</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Sign the agreements</span><em>Online, one for all your cars</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>One registry visit</span><em>We fill in the forms and come with you</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Tracker and insurance</span><em>We install it and add the car</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Photos and listing</span><em>Live within 1 business day</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Right after you apply, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Read your agreements</b>: both agreements, filled in from your application, marked &quot;Terms pending approval&quot;. The fees and the Revenue Share read Pending approval until we set them, and the Sign button stays off.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When your terms are ready, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b>. Everything is filled in from your application: check the short list of key values (each has a <b class="gd-ui">Fix</b> link) and open any document to read it in full.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: say you read the documents, initial the three confirmations, tick the two consents and draw your signature. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Sign all</b>. A code to your phone or email is optional (<b class="gd-ui">Verify by code</b>); it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on. One signature covers every document, in about two minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Pay the upfront invoice: the first and last month&#39;s insurance fee for each car (see chapter 4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Upload what each car&#39;s checklist asks for: the ownership permit, the lender&#39;s permission if it is financed or leased, and insurance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Sign Forms C and D (filled in for you) on screen, with your witnesses beside you on the same device: Form C with one witness, Form D with two (see chapter 5).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-if-we-need-a-little-more" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If we need a little more</h2><p class="gd-p">Sometimes we need one more document before we can approve your application, for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an email, and Home shows &quot;We need a little more&quot; with the list and any note from our team.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Upload what is asked, or write Your answer, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send my answer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">We review it within 1 business day. Once we approve your application, you get an email and Home shows Check and sign.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No typing the VIN: press <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and point your phone at the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b> and take a photo of it. Check the VIN shown before you continue.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Photos:</b> on your car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> takes any number at once, in any order. We sort them, put the outside photos on our studio background and touch up the inside ones. Photos that fit no shot go in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>. At least 10 are needed.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-a-fleet-supplier-lease-your-cars-to-carmacars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</h2><p class="gd-p">For a corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars for a fixed amount a month. You pay CarmaCars no fees: no invoices, no debits.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span> and press <b class="gd-ui">A corporation with a fleet? Lease your cars to us as a fleet supplier</b> (or choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b> in the application, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">About you: the corporation&#39;s legal name and number, its registered address, and the signing officer&#39;s name and title.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For each car: type the VIN (the year, make and model fill in), then the plate, and mark the car <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it needs work). Each tier shows its lease a month. The tier is set when you add the car and does not change.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Say who the car is registered to now: <b class="gd-ui">My corporation</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Me or another officer, personally</b> (it moves into your corporation), or <b class="gd-ui">A seller: the corporation is buying it</b>. For the last two, enter the name and address on the ownership and the transfer or sale date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue</b>, check the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Submit application</b>. The ServiceOntario forms each car needs are filled in for you at once, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: the lease to CarmaCars (CarmaCars holds the plates while it leases the car) and, for a car not yet registered to your corporation, the transfer into it. A seller signs the transfer on the back of the ownership. Only the empty boxes are filled. Sign each one on screen under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, then print it and sign it in ink at ServiceOntario.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">In your owner portal, open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then each car, and upload its ownership (registration) copy.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We check each car. Once we approve it, it is on the lease at its tier and Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b>: you sign the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Form B (the lease summary) in the owner portal, on screen (there is no paper option). Form D (the limited power of attorney) is in your Documents too: you sign it on screen with two witnesses beside you, and CarmaCars signs its Part 2 at the same moment.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Home and <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> show <b class="gd-ui">Your fleet lease</b>: each car, its tier, its lease a month and the next payment date. The lease is paid on the 10th for the month before, with your statement; the first payment comes at least one full month after the car goes on the lease, and part months are paid by the day. Add more cars from your owner portal the same way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">You sign your agreement before any car comes over. As soon as your profile has your legal or corporation name, your address and, for a corporation, the signing officer and title, your agreement is made from it: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement (with the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement it relies on) if you lease cars to CarmaCars, the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement otherwise. No car is needed.</p><p class="gd-p">Your owner portal home shows six steps: Your profile, Sign the agreement, Add your cars, Photos and inspection, Approved, Delivered. The current step has one button; press it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Sign the agreement.</b> Read and sign opens it, filled in from your profile. You sign once on screen; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Add your cars.</b> One at a time, or as a list of VINs from Cars &gt; Add cars from a VIN list (a fleet supplier gives each car its tier and plate there). Each car goes on Schedule A of your agreement as a numbered entry, and you confirm each batch with one signature (Confirm my cars). Its government forms are made at the same moment.</li><li>A car is approved, delivered or rented only once your agreement and its Schedule A entry are signed. If CarmaCars approved it before you signed, it goes through by itself the moment you sign.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">Your car&#39;s steps, one at a time</h3><p class="gd-p">Once a car is on its way, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Your next step</b> and each car&#39;s page shows <b class="gd-ui">Your car&#39;s steps</b>: every step of its onboarding, the one thing to do now with its button, what to bring, where to go and how long it takes. You are emailed and texted when a step is yours.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">The route.</b> <em>Transfer</em>: the car&#39;s registration moves into CarmaCars&#39; name. <em>Co-Registrant</em>: CarmaCars is added beside you. <em>Lease</em>: your corporation keeps the car and leases it to CarmaCars (no title transfer). An individual who leases through a new Owner Corporation first sets it up: Incorporate now opens our online incorporation partner (about 20 minutes), then upload the certificate.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The steps.</b> Application, Terms approved, Agreements signed, Documents uploaded (your driver&#39;s licence, both sides of the ownership permit, your insurance slip and, if the car is financed, the lender&#39;s payout letter; a corporation gives its corporate documents), Ownership transfer, New registration uploaded, Plate and insurance on the fleet policy, Inspected and photographed, Listed.</li><li>Ownership transfer. Press <b class="gd-ui">Find a ServiceOntario centre</b>, book a time, then <b class="gd-ui">I booked it</b> with the time and the centre. Bring your licence, the original ownership permit, proof of insurance, the filled Form A and transfer documents (Documents &gt; Government forms), the Used Vehicle Information Package and the Safety Standards Certificate when the step lists them. You pay the registry&#39;s charges at the counter unless your Vehicle Schedule says CarmaCars pays them. After the counter, tick that the fees are paid and press <b class="gd-ui">Transfer done</b>, then upload the new ownership permit on the car&#39;s page.</li><li>A step that waits on CarmaCars says <b class="gd-ui">With CarmaCars</b>: nothing to do on your side.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-your-steps-one-at-a-time" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your steps, one at a time</h2><p class="gd-p">Your home page shows your steps as a line of checkpoints: each one ticks when it is done, the one to do now is marked in red, and a tap on any step says what it needs and how long it takes. When the last one is done, your car is listed and earning.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'rewards', 'chapter', 'fees-payments-and-payouts', '**Rewards** in the menu shows everything you get as an owner, with your codes, your progress and your history.

## While your car is out

1. On dates your own car is on rent, in service or in a claim, your code gives you 20% off another CarmaCars car. Press **Copy the code**, then **Find a car**, and type the code in the promo code box of your request.
2. You are the driver. The licence check, the rental agreement and the deposit are the same as for any renter. The code does not work on exotic cars, partner cars or your own car.
3. If your car is being repaired for something CarmaCars caused, press **Ask for a free upgrade**, choose the car and say what happened. An Admin answers on this page and by email. When it is approved you get a one-time code.

## Friends and family

1. Share your **code**, your **link** or your **QR code**. A friend gets 10% off their first rental.
2. You earn 20% of the rental charge on that first rental. It shows on your statement once the trip is complete.
3. The page counts the friends who rented and what you earned.

## Refer an owner

Share the link under **Refer an owner**. When the owner you referred has had a car live for 30 days, a $100 credit goes on your next statement as its own line.

## Merch kits

1. At 6 months with CarmaCars the **CarmaCars merch kit** is ready, and at 12 months the **Premium merch kit**. The bar shows how far you are.
2. Nothing is sent by itself. Press **Redeem my merch kit**, check the address, choose a shirt size and press **Confirm and redeem**.
3. The kit then shows **Getting ready**, and **Shipped** with the tracking number once it is on its way. We email you at each step.

## Birthday credit and perks

1. On your birthday you get a $25 rental credit as a code, good for 60 days. Add your birthday under Account if we do not have it.
2. You have priority support: your calls, texts and messages are answered first. You also hear about new programs before anyone else.

**Your rewards so far** lists every credit, kit and code. Credits are a line on your statement. Your Revenue Share and fees do not change.', 'Rewards', 'Your discounts, your friends and family code, credits and merch kits.',
