select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'admin-call', 'chapter', 'hiring', null, 'The weekly Admin call', 'The deck, the decisions to take, the call and its invite.',
  'The Admin call is the weekly call of the Admins (Team > Admin call). By default it is every Sunday at 7:00 pm Toronto time, for 60 minutes: change the day, the time or the length with **Change the day or time** on the page, or in Settings > Program settings (Admin call). Every Admin gets the weekly calendar invite by email (a calendar file: accept it once and it repeats), and an update when the time changes. **Add to my calendar (every week)** downloads the same event.

## The deck

The deck builds itself the day before the call and again three hours before, from the live data; **Build again** rebuilds it any time. An alert reaches the Admins an hour before. One slide a section:

1. Shifts for the coming week: what is published, the spots still open and each claim.
2. Staff hours (last 7 days) and the staff payouts owed.
3. Academy progress, person by person.
4. Hiring: new applications, interviews booked, waiting for a decision, hired, and the interview no-shows by first name.
5. Social media: the posts planned for the coming week, those still to approve, last week''s posts and figures.
6. The numbers of the last 7 days: bookings, revenue booked, occupancy, real visitors, conversion, leads by source and sales by rep.
7. Owners: applications, cars onboarding, statements to approve, payouts due, cars in arrears.
8. Deposits to release or keep.
9. Insurance billing and replacement rentals.
10. Claims.
11. Prepared money actions (from Claude).
12. Tolls and tickets.
13. Fleet: cars out of service, maintenance To dos, cars free all next week, cars missing photos.
14. To dos on the Admin queue that need a decision.

## Approve and Deny

Every decision is on its slide with its two buttons, decided once (the name of the Admin who pressed it shows):

- **A shift claim**: Approve keeps it; Take off the shift removes the person from it.
- **A To do**: Decline closes it with your reason; Approve leaves it open, marked approved.
- **A prepared money action**: Approve marks it approved and urgent; Decline closes it. No money moves from the deck: it moves only from its own screen.
- **A deposit** (Release or Keep) and **an owner payout** (Pay it or Hold it): the decision goes to Finance as a To do, done in Deposit reviews or Payouts with their usual checks.

Add a note to any slide. **Join the call** opens the call in the site, with the deck beside it; only Admins can join it.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The Admin call is the weekly call of the Admins (Team &gt; Admin call). By default it is every Sunday at 7:00 pm Toronto time, for 60 minutes: change the day, the time or the length with <b class="gd-ui">Change the day or time</b> on the page, or in Settings &gt; Program settings (Admin call). Every Admin gets the weekly calendar invite by email (a calendar file: accept it once and it repeats), and an update when the time changes. <b class="gd-ui">Add to my calendar (every week)</b> downloads the same event.</p><section class="gd-task" id="admin-call-the-deck" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The deck</h2><p class="gd-p">The deck builds itself the day before the call and again three hours before, from the live data; <b class="gd-ui">Build again</b> rebuilds it any time. An alert reaches the Admins an hour before. One slide a section:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Shifts for the coming week: what is published, the spots still open and each claim.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Staff hours (last 7 days) and the staff payouts owed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Academy progress, person by person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Hiring: new applications, interviews booked, waiting for a decision, hired, and the interview no-shows by first name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Social media: the posts planned for the coming week, those still to approve, last week&#39;s posts and figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers of the last 7 days: bookings, revenue booked, occupancy, real visitors, conversion, leads by source and sales by rep.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Owners: applications, cars onboarding, statements to approve, payouts due, cars in arrears.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits to release or keep.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Insurance billing and replacement rentals.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Claims.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Prepared money actions (from Claude).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet: cars out of service, maintenance To dos, cars free all next week, cars missing photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">To dos on the Admin queue that need a decision.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="admin-call-approve-and-deny" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve and Deny</h2><p class="gd-p">Every decision is on its slide with its two buttons, decided once (the name of the Admin who pressed it shows):</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">A shift claim</b>: Approve keeps it; Take off the shift removes the person from it.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">A To do</b>: Decline closes it with your reason; Approve leaves it open, marked approved.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">A prepared money action</b>: Approve marks it approved and urgent; Decline closes it. No money moves from the deck: it moves only from its own screen.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">A deposit</b> (Release or Keep) and <b class="gd-ui">an owner payout</b> (Pay it or Hold it): the decision goes to Finance as a To do, done in Deposit reviews or Payouts with their usual checks.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Add a note to any slide. <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens the call in the site, with the deck beside it; only Admins can join it.</p></section>');
